  "generated_text": "To find the sum of the solutions of the quadratic equation \\(-32x^2 + 84x + 135 = 0\\), we can use the properties of quadratic equations. For a quadratic equation of the form \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), the sum of the solutions is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of the solutions} = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nIn the given equation \\(-32x^2 + 84x + 135 = 0\\), we identify the coefficients as follows:\n- \\(a = -32\\)\n- \\(b = 84\\)\n- \\(c = 135\\)\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of the solutions:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of the solutions} = -\\frac{84}{-32}\n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify the fraction:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{84}{-32} = \\frac{84}{32} = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the solutions of the equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
